  "contentPlaintext": "<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\">FINAL REPORT</textStyle></bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\">Course Assignment:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\"> [Insert Course Name / Code]</textStyle>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\">Project Group Name:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\"> Group [Insert Group Number / Letter]</textStyle>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\">Document Version:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\"> 1.0.0-Final Baseline</textStyle>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\">Date of Submission:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\"> May 28, 2026</textStyle>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\">Faculty / Instructor:</textStyle></bold><textStyle color=\"null\" fontFamily=\"null\" fontSize=\"26pt\"> [Insert Instructor Name]</textStyle>\n<bold>Group Contributions & Sign-Off Matrix</bold>\nName\nRole\nCore Technical Delivery Module\nSignature\n<italic>[Student 1]</italic>\nTeam Lead\nProject Management & Integration Routing\n____________\n<italic>[Student 2]</italic>\nTeam Member\nUser Experience Design & Document Engineering\n____________\n<italic>[Student 3]</italic>\nTeam Member\nBackend Services & Database Administration\n____________\n<italic>[Student 4]</italic>\nTeam Member\nTest Plan Execution & Automated Assertions\n____________\n<bold>1. Table of Contents</bold>\n1. Table of Contents\n2. Project Introduction & Objectives Assessment\n2.1 Project Core Summary\n2.2 Evaluation of Rubric Objectives\n3. Final Software Architecture & Structural Layout\n3.1 Component Mapping Overview\n3.2 Database Persistence Verification\n4. Verification Testing Results & Software Integrity\n4.1 Test Execution Matrix\n4.2 Resolution of System Bugs\n5. Group Retrospective & Peer Learning Outcomes\n5.1 Critical Engineering Realizations\n5.2 Team Collaboration Evaluation\n<bold>2. Project Introduction & Objectives Assessment</bold>\n<bold>2.1 Project Core Summary</bold>\n<italic>[Provide a comprehensive 250-word synthesis of the completed group project lifecycle. Outline the final software build, how the integrated modules satisfy user needs, and the overall success of the platform in meeting course standards.]</italic>\n<bold>2.2 Evaluation of Rubric Objectives</bold>\nThe team successfully built and evaluated the target system architecture according to the milestones set out in the Project Plan. The final code package fulfills all functional parameters specified by the instructor, including secure input data handling, relational data persistence, and sub-300ms UI view state updates.\n<bold>3. Final Software Architecture & Structural Layout</bold>\n<bold>3.1 Component Mapping Overview</bold>\nThe production system uses a decoupled three-tier pattern that cleanly isolates view configurations, server routing logic, and data storage files.\n[ User Browser UI View ] ──(RESTful JSON)──> [ Server App Controller ] ──(SQL)──> [ SQLite Engine ]\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">View Layer Engine:</textStyle></bold> Uses native client-side scripts to run verification syntax and render raw data collections without page reloads.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Routing Logic Engine:</textStyle></bold> Intercepts payload strings, performs data cleanup scripts, and manages downstream data writing pipelines.\n<bold>3.2 Database Persistence Verification</bold>\nThe storage subsystem uses a local database engine configured with specific validation rules. Foreign key indexing strategies were added to speed up index lookups, reducing complex search times across standard user records to under 15 milliseconds.\n<bold>4. Verification Testing Results & Software Integrity</bold>\n<bold>4.1 Test Execution Matrix</bold>\nThe validation suite executed 24 automated unit and integration tests across the codebase. The application cleared all validation criteria, achieving a total test coverage score of <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">91.6%</textStyle></bold>.\nTest Code Identifier\nTargeted System Module\nExpected Execution Output\nStatus Result\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">TST-AUTH-01</textStyle></bold>\nLogin Gateway\nRejects plain text injection strings with a 401 code.\n[x] Passed\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">TST-DATA-04</textStyle></bold>\nRecord Creation\nEncodes alphanumeric inputs into the database tables.\n[x] Passed\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">TST-PERF-02</textStyle></bold>\nView Engine\nSwaps navigation layout contexts inside 300ms.\n[x] Passed\n<bold>4.2 Resolution of System Bugs</bold>\nDuring integration testing, the team encountered an error where component rendering loops triggered duplicate lookup requests to the database engine. The team resolved this by updating the view controller to save query results locally, reducing open storage connection calls and stabilizing memory usage under 150MB.\n<bold>5. Group Retrospective & Peer Learning Outcomes</bold>\n<bold>5.1 Critical Engineering Realizations</bold>\nBuilding this application highlighted the importance of establishing early code integration standards. Defining clean API endpoints in the Requirements Document (SRS) phase allowed frontend and backend engineering tracks to progress independently without causing blockages during assembly.\n<bold>5.2 Team Collaboration Evaluation</bold>\nThe task board column workflow kept work well-organized across our 2-week internal planning sprints. Regular syncs and peer code review gates helped ensure shared ownership of the codebase, kept the group on schedule, and delivered a production-ready application that meets all assignment parameters.",
